.TH TQUERY 1 "August 2026" "tquery 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tquery \- interactive terminal visualizer & query engine for JSON data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tquery
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIJQ_EXPRESSION\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.br
\fBcurl\fR ... | \fBtquery\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIJQ_EXPRESSION\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tquery
is a fast, Unix-native terminal utility designed to solve the "human interface problem" when working with JSON data in the terminal.
Instead of dumping dense or formatted raw JSON text, \fBtquery\fR parses raw JSON streams, normalizes nested objects and arrays, evaluates embedded \fBjq\fR queries natively, and renders beautiful ANSI color-coded ASCII/Unicode tables, hierarchical trees, and markdown documents.

It automatically unwraps top-level REST API wrappers (such as \fI{"data": [...]}\fR, \fI{"items": [...]}\fR, or \fI{"models": [...]}\fR) into readable data tables without requiring manual jq array selectors.

\fBtquery\fR also features an interactive Terminal User Interface (TUI) mode triggered with \fB\-i\fR or when launched interactively, featuring real-time live jq query filtering, keyboard scrolling, view mode switching, and row inspection.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Set output formatting mode (aliases accepted: \fBmd\fR for markdown and \fBraw\fR for json; unknown values are rejected with an error). Supported formats:
.RS
.IP \fBtable\fR 4
(Default) Color-coded Unicode ASCII table with auto-aligned columns and syntax-colored primitives.
.IP \fBmarkdown\fR 4
GitHub-Flavored Markdown (GFM) pipe table.
.IP \fBcsv\fR 4
Comma-separated values data stream.
.IP \fBtsv\fR 4
Tab-separated values data stream.
.IP \fBtree\fR 4
Indented ASCII tree structure displaying nested keys and types.
.IP \fBjson\fR 4
Pretty-printed JSON object output.
.RE

.TP
\fB\-<number>\fR, \fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fINUM\fR
Limit the maximum number of output rows displayed (e.g. \fBtquery \-10\fR or \fBtquery \-l 5\fR).

.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
Launch interactive TUI mode with a live jq query prompt, keyboard navigation, view switcher, and row detail inspector overlay drawer.

.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-no-headers\fR
Omit header rows in table, markdown, and CSV formats.

.TP
\fB\-\-no-unwrap\fR
Disable automatic root array un-wrapping for top-level REST API wrapper keys (e.g. \fIdata\fR, \fIitems\fR, \fIresults\fR).

.TP
\fB\-\-no-color\fR
Disable ANSI color formatting in output.

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print software version and exit.

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display comprehensive CLI usage information and examples.

.SH JQ QUERY ENGINE
.B tquery\fR embeds a pure-Go implementation of \fBjq\fR (\fBgojq\fR). No external \fBjq\fR executable is required.
You can pass any standard \fBjq\fR filter as a positional argument.

.B Examples of valid JQ expressions:
.RS
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB.data[]\fR - Extract array elements
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB.data[] | {id, owned_by}\fR - Construct object containing specific fields
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB.models[] | select(.created > 1600000000)\fR - Filter array elements by condition
.RE

.SH INTERACTIVE TUI NAVIGATION
When \fBtquery\fR is executed with \fB\-i\fR or launched interactively:
.TP
\fBType Text\fR
Updates the live \fBjq >\fR query prompt and re-renders table/tree views instantaneously.
.TP
\fBTab\fR
Cycles active view mode (\fBTable\fR \-> \fBTree\fR \-> \fBJSON\fR).
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Pops open the \fBInspect Row Detail\fR overlay drawer for the selected table row, presenting full key-value pairs and nested objects.
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Closes the Inspect Row Detail overlay.
.TP
\fBUp / Down / Vim (k / j)\fR
Scrolls table rows or viewport content.
.TP
\fBCtrl+C / q\fR
Exits the application.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBVisualize REST API response as a table:\fR
$ curl \-s https://inference.dahl.global/v1/models | tquery

.TP
\fBFilter REST API response with JQ query into table:\fR
$ curl \-s https://inference.dahl.global/v1/models | tquery '.data[] | {id, owned_by}'

.TP
\fBConvert JSON file to Markdown table:\fR
$ tquery \-f markdown '.data' data.json

.TP
\fBExport JSON file to CSV:\fR
$ tquery \-f csv data.json > output.csv

.TP
\fBDisplay JSON file as a tree:\fR
$ tquery \-f tree config.json

.TP
\fBLaunch interactive TUI explorer on JSON file:\fR
$ tquery \-i payload.json

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jq (1),
.BR curl (1)

.SH AUTHOR
Created for terminal productivity and JSON data exploration.
